{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub","id":1122743,"title":"Haberdasher's Requiem Homebrew Hub","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-30T10:50:19-07:00","id":1122743,"title":"Haberdasher's Requiem Homebrew Hub","content":"Hey everybody! I've decided to create a single page where people can find my homebrew material, whether it be my 2e interpretations and conversions of 1e material, or homebrew bloodlines that I create from scratch, which will definitely be incoming. Bloodline conversions will be organized by book, alphabetically, so that people can find them more easily. Currently, I've completed conversions for all of the bloodlines in the 1e core book and the clan books, and I'm working on conversions for bloodlines from the covenant books.<br /> <br /> Original bloodlines will be kept separate from the converted bloodlines.<br /> <br /> These homebrews are meant to be used by both Players and Storytellers, so don't hesitate to use one of my creations, or use them as inspiration for your own homebrew material! I only ask that you tell me when you use my stuff (and how it went, I love details!) and give me a shoutout if you use one of my homebrews as a starting point for your own and you post it to the forums.<br /> <br /> If you want, I can include brief descriptions of bloodlines here on the forums in case you're looking for a particular bloodline, but can't remember what it's called or aren't familiar with 1e but want some bloodlines to spice up a Chronicle. I will always add a brief description of my original bloodlines, since people <br /> won't have the benefit of a 1e version to know what the bloodline's concept is at glance.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Converted Bloodlines</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>\u200bVampire the Requiem: 1st Edition Core</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/950657-bloodline-conversion-bruja\">Bruja</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/955064-bloodline-conversion-burakumin\">Burakumin</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/959429-bloodline-conversion-malkavians\">Malkavians</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/972027-bloodline-conversion-morbus\">Morbus</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/976261-bloodline-conversion-toreador\">Toreador</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>Clan Book: Daeva</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/933188-bloodline-erzs\u00e9bet-2e\">Erzs\u00e9bet</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>Clan Book: Gangrel</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/984718-bloodline-conversion-the-hounds-of-actaeon\">The Hounds of Actaeon</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/988439-bloodline-conversion-mabry\">Mabry</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>Clan Book: Mekhet</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1019279-bloodline-conversion-mnemosyne\">Mnemosyne</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1022330-bloodline-conversion-norvegi\">Norvegi</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>\u200bClan Book: Nosferatu</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.